      "notYetCorrected": [
        {
          "date": "2026-10-27",
          "was": "Nothing joins a table to the parts of a study area, so the 32 mortality rates and the 32 named boundaries cannot colour one another. That join is the choropleth this example argues for in prose.",
          "why": "That sentence was true when the pin was written and false from 2026-10-25, when join_table_to_area shipped and the bundle gained a working choropleth workflow. The example repository corrected its own README the same day -- it says \"Both are now false\" and keeps the old sentence as the record of what the join was built to close -- and this field did not. THIS FIELD IS THE ONE A READER SEES: renderExampleCatalog prints it as \"Not yet: ...\" on the catalog card, so the deployed application advertised the example as missing the very workflow it ships. Found 2026-10-27 while asking what was left of the join work."
        },
        {
          "date": "2026-10-31",
          "was": "The georeferenced plate and the three traced supply zones in geo/ are still for other tools: nothing in Fieldwork reads a raster plate or those zones onto a canvas.",
          "why": "The plate half was true when the pin was written and false from 2026-10-27, when map_image_input shipped and the bundle wired Map 2 as ground under the choropleth. This is the SECOND time this field has advertised the example as missing a workflow it ships, and the second time it was found by somebody working on the thing rather than by a check -- the bundle is verified byte for byte and this sentence is verified by nobody. Found 2026-10-31 while giving the plate a workflow of its own. The zones half is still true and stays."
        }
      ],
